# Q, Stacking the Deck {2}{R}{R}. Its enters trigger shuffles Bot1's library and exiles from the top until a nonland card:
# Crimson Kobolds is the library's only nonland, so it is the card exiled however the shuffle falls. That card gains
# "Exile a card from your hand: Create a copy of this card. You may cast the copy. Activate only during your turn and only if
# this card is exiled." - Bot1 pays its cost by exiling the Swamp from its hand, leaving the Mountain there (CR 602.2b,
# 601.2h), and casts the copy, which becomes a token (CR 707.12b). Then Bot2's Binding Negotiation puts the exiled card
# into Bot1's graveyard, and the ability is offered no more: only a card in exile can use it (CR 113.6b, 400.7).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
